<title>JAPAN: KYOKUTO CLEARED TO RAISE CRUDE PROCESSING CAPACITY.</title>
<headline>KYOKUTO CLEARED TO RAISE CRUDE PROCESSING CAPACITY.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kyokuto Petroleum Industries Ltd said on Tuesday it received approval from the Trade Ministry to raise the crude processing capacity at its Chiba plant near Tokyo by 12,000 barrels-per-day (bpd) to 155,000 bpd.</p>
<p>&quot;We plan to resume operations at the plant with the expanded capacity on August 16,&quot; a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>The Chiba plant has been closed since July 16 for scheduled maintenance.</p>
<p>Kyokuto Petroleum is owned equally by Mobil Sekiyu KK, a Japanese unit of Mobil Corp, and Mitsui Oil &amp; Gas Co Ltd.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Energy Desk +81-3-3432-8837</p>
</text>
